* Junction and end-cap residues for a tetra-PEG network built from the
* CHARMM C35r ether force field (PEGM strands). Not part of C35r.
*

read rtf card append
* PEJ, the tetrafunctional junction: a quaternary carbon bonded to the C1 or
* C2 carbons of four PEGM strands (a pentaerythritol-type core), typed CC30A
* with charge 0, as the quaternary carbon of the CHARMM alkanes.
* PEGC, a methyl cap for a dangling strand end: the atoms and charges of
* the C35r MET1 patch (CE CC33A -0.27, three HCA3A 0.09).
*
36 1

RESI PEJ          0.00
GROUP
ATOM C    CC30A    0.00

RESI PEGC         0.00
GROUP
ATOM C    CC33A   -0.27
ATOM H1   HCA3A    0.09
ATOM H2   HCA3A    0.09
ATOM H3   HCA3A    0.09
BOND C H1  C H2  C H3

END

read param card flex append
* Terms C35r does not define around a CC30A carbon bonded to a PEGM
* CH2-O. Parameters by analogy (not fitted), each copied from the C35r term
* named beside it: the ether O-C-C angle and torsions with the quaternary
* carbon in place of a CH2. Every other term of the network is C35r's own.
*

ANGLES
CC30A    CC32A    OC30A     45.00    111.50  ! = OC30A CC32A CC32A (DEET)

DIHEDRALS
CC32A    CC30A    CC32A    OC30A     0.16    1   180.0  ! = OC30A CC32A CC32A CC32A (MPET)
CC32A    CC30A    CC32A    OC30A     0.39    2     0.0  ! = OC30A CC32A CC32A CC32A (MPET)
CC30A    CC32A    OC30A    CC32A     0.57    1     0.0  ! = CC32A CC32A OC30A CC32A (DME)
CC30A    CC32A    OC30A    CC32A     0.29    2     0.0  ! = CC32A CC32A OC30A CC32A (DME)
CC30A    CC32A    OC30A    CC32A     0.43    3     0.0  ! = CC32A CC32A OC30A CC32A (DME)

END

return
